.TH HALREPORT "1" "2026-08-03" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
halreport \- collect one diagnostic bundle for a support question
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halreport
[\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR] [\fB\-\-ini\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-stdout\fR]
[\fB\-\-journal\-lines\fR \fIN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBhalreport\fR gathers, in one command, what is needed to answer a support
question about a machine: versions, the host and real\-time environment, the
configuration that was actually loaded, live HAL topology and thread timing,
machine state, and logs.
.PP
It runs on the machine, because much of what matters (kernel, distro, INI and
HAL files, journal) is not reachable over the REST API. It contacts a running
\fBgomc\-server\fR for the HAL and machine sections and falls back to the
host\-only sections when none is reachable \(em a machine that will not start is
exactly when a report is wanted.
.PP
The bundle contains the text report, the INI file and the local files it names
(HAL files, tool table, panel XML), the \fBgomc\-server\fR journal and the tail
of \fBdmesg\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
Bundle path. Default \fB./halreport\-<host>\-<timestamp>.tar.gz\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-ini\fR \fIFILE\fR
INI file to record. Default \fB$INI_FILE_NAME\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stdout\fR
Write the text report to standard output and create no bundle.
.TP
\fB\-\-journal\-lines\fR \fIN\fR
Journal lines to capture. Default 2000.
.SH "SIGNAL UPDATE ORDER"
The most diagnostic section lists, for each signal, the pins on it and the
thread slot servicing each one. A reader with a lower slot number than its
writer sees the previous cycle's value. The servicing function is resolved from
the component that owns the pin, as published by HAL, so a component exporting
several functions has all of them listed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBGMC_REST_URL\fR
Base URL of the gomc server (default \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:5080\fR).
.TP
\fBGMC_INSTANCE\fR
Task instance to address (default \fBmilltask\fR).
.TP
\fBINI_FILE_NAME\fR
INI file recorded when \fB\-\-ini\fR is not given.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBhalcmd(1)\fR, \fBlinuxcnc(1)\fR
